# Focus & tabIndex Policy

## Core Rules

### tabIndex values — only 0 and -1, NEVER positive

| Value | Meaning | When to use |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `tabIndex={0}` | In natural tab order | Custom interactive elements (`div` acting as button, custom widget) |
| `tabIndex={-1}` | Programmatically focusable, NOT in tab order | Scroll containers, group wrappers, focus targets for `element.focus()` |
| `tabIndex={1+}` | **FORBIDDEN** | Never. Breaks natural DOM order, creates accessibility nightmare |
| *(no tabIndex)* | Default behavior | Native interactive elements (`<button>`, `<a>`, `<input>`) — already focusable |

### Decision tree

```
Is it a native interactive element (button, a, input, select, textarea)?
  YES → Do NOT add tabIndex. It's already focusable.
  NO  → Should it be keyboard-accessible?
          YES → tabIndex={0} + role + aria-label + keydown handler
          NO  → Should code .focus() it programmatically?
                  YES → tabIndex={-1}
                  NO  → No tabIndex needed
```

## Focus Zones (F6 cycling)

The app is divided into focus zones — keyboard users press **F6** to cycle between them (like Slack, Teams, VS Code):

| Zone | `data-focus-zone` | ARIA role | Component |
|------|------------------|-----------|-----------|
| Top bar | `topbar` | `banner` | `TopBar` |
| Sidebar | `sidebar` | `navigation` | `Sidebar` |
| Main content | `main` | `main` | `<main>` in Layout |
| Composer | `composer` | `form` | `MessageComposer` |
| Info panel | `panel` | `complementary` | `RightDrawer` |

```tsx
<header data-focus-zone="topbar" role="banner" aria-label="Top bar">
<aside data-focus-zone="sidebar" role="navigation" aria-label="Chat list">
<main data-focus-zone="main" role="main" aria-label="Content">
<div data-focus-zone="composer" role="form" aria-label="Message composer">
<aside data-focus-zone="panel" role="complementary" aria-label="Info panel">
```

**F6** cycles forward, **Shift+F6** cycles backward. Implemented in `shared/lib/focus.ts`.

## Focus Trap (Modals/Dialogs)

When a modal or dialog is open, focus must be trapped inside:

```tsx
import { useFocusTrap } from "~/shared/lib/focus";

function SearchModal({ open }) {
  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  useFocusTrap(ref, open);

  return <div ref={ref} role="dialog" aria-modal="true">...</div>;
}
```

Behavior:
- On open: saves previous focus, moves to first focusable inside
- Tab wraps within modal (last → first, shift+tab first → last)
- On close: restores focus to the element that opened the modal

## Roving tabIndex (Lists, Toolbars, Tabs)

For lists where arrow keys navigate between items:

```tsx
import { useRovingTabindex } from "~/shared/lib/focus";

function ChatList() {
  const listRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  useRovingTabindex(listRef, { orientation: "vertical", loop: true });

  return (
    <div ref={listRef} role="listbox">
      <div role="option" data-roving-item>Chat 1</div>
      <div role="option" data-roving-item>Chat 2</div>
      <div role="option" data-roving-item>Chat 3</div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Behavior:
- First item: `tabIndex={0}`, rest: `tabIndex={-1}`
- Arrow keys move focus between items
- Home/End jump to first/last
- Only ONE item in the group is in the tab order at any time

### Where to use roving tabindex

| Widget | Orientation | Items |
|--------|-------------|-------|
| Section tabs in TopBar | horizontal | `role="tab"` |
| Folder rail | vertical | `role="option"` |
| Chat list in sidebar | vertical | `role="option"` |
| Message action toolbar | horizontal | `role="menuitem"` |
| Emoji reaction bar | horizontal | `role="menuitem"` |

## Skip-to-Content Link

A visually hidden link appears at the top of the page when Tab is pressed:

```
[Tab] → "Skip to content" link appears → [Enter] → focus moves to main content
```

Implemented in `app/app.tsx` with `.skip-link` CSS class.

## ARIA Landmarks

Every major section has a landmark role:

```
role="application"      → root app container
role="banner"           → top bar (header)
role="navigation"       → sidebar
role="main"             → page content
role="form"             → message composer
role="complementary"    → right info panel
role="dialog"           → modals (with aria-modal="true")
```

## Module Reference

```
shared/lib/focus.ts
├── initFocusManagement()      — F6 zone cycling setup
├── focusZone(name)            — focus first element in a zone
├── cycleToNextZone()          — F6 handler
├── cycleToPrevZone()          — Shift+F6 handler
├── getFocusableElements(el)   — query all focusable children
├── getFirstFocusable(el)      — first focusable child
├── getLastFocusable(el)       — last focusable child
├── useFocusTrap(ref, active)  — trap focus in modal
├── useRovingTabindex(ref, opts) — arrow key navigation in lists
├── useFocusRestore()          — save/restore focus pair
└── focusMainContent()         — skip-to-content target
```

## Rules for AI Agent

### MUST

1. **Never use `tabIndex > 0`** — always 0 or -1
2. **Native elements first** — prefer `<button>` over `<div onClick>`. If you must use div, add `tabIndex={0}`, `role="button"`, `onKeyDown` for Enter/Space
3. **Every interactive custom element** needs: `tabIndex`, `role`, `aria-label`, keyboard handler
4. **Every modal/dialog** must use `useFocusTrap` and `role="dialog" aria-modal="true"`
5. **Every list with arrow navigation** must use `useRovingTabindex`
6. **Focus zones** — new major UI sections need `data-focus-zone`

### MUST NOT

- Do NOT remove `outline` on `:focus-visible` — it's critical for keyboard users
- Do NOT add `tabIndex={0}` to non-interactive containers (div, section, article)
- Do NOT use `autofocus` attribute — use `useEffect` + `ref.focus()` instead
- Do NOT break tab order with `tabIndex > 0`
- Do NOT trap focus without an escape mechanism (Escape key)

### Checklist for new components

- [ ] Interactive elements are keyboard-accessible (Enter/Space activate)
- [ ] Custom widgets have appropriate `role` and `aria-*` attributes
- [ ] Lists use roving tabindex if navigable by arrow keys
- [ ] Modals trap focus and restore on close
- [ ] No `tabIndex > 0` anywhere
- [ ] Focus is visible (`:focus-visible` outline)
